  "verbalization": "Arundinol B is shown to interact with SNU-387, which is a compound that acts as a target for multiple metabolites, including (1S,3R,6S,8R,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, all of which target Carboxylesterase 2. The evidence suggests that Arundinol B may inhibit Carboxylesterase 2 through a mechanism involving the interaction with SNU-387, which is a known substrate of the enzyme. The final scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, with the shared target of SNU-387 across the three paths supporting a unified mechanism. The presence of multiple metabolites targeting Carboxylesterase 2 suggests that the enzyme may be involved in the metabolism of these compounds, and Arundinol B may act as a modulator of this process. The evidence is consistent and supports a mechanistic link between Arundinol B and Carboxylesterase 2, with the core mechanism likely involving the inhibition of the enzyme through the interaction with its substrates.",
